[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3239406512","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110112#issuecomment-3239406512","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110112","id":3239406512,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BFWuw","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-30T17:06:32Z","updated_at":"2025-08-30T17:06:32Z","body":"I think it would make more sense if the undo/redo action ended up being `Duplicate Node(s)` instead of the transform, since in terms of importance of what is actually is happening within the single action is node(s) are being duplicated first and foremost and how it's being transformed is secondary and not worth mentioning. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3239406512/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3239411526","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110112#issuecomment-3239411526","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110112","id":3239411526,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BFX9G","user":{"login":"winston-yallow","id":44872771,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODcyNzcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44872771?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow","html_url":"https://github.com/winston-yallow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-30T17:17:09Z","updated_at":"2025-08-30T17:17:09Z","body":"good point, adjusted the name of the undo/redo action :+1: ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3239411526/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3239443829","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110112#issuecomment-3239443829","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110112","id":3239443829,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BFf11","user":{"login":"winston-yallow","id":44872771,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODcyNzcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44872771?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow","html_url":"https://github.com/winston-yallow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-30T18:25:39Z","updated_at":"2025-08-30T18:25:39Z","body":"I thought about that and tried it at first, but the code became a bit convoluted. The issue is that `SceneTreeDock` mixes node duplication logic with undo/redo logic, and separating this would mean splitting it into three parts: duplication, tracking the duplication changes, then creating the undo/redo based on the changes. It is possible, but at least to me it seemed to introduce a lot of unnecessary complexity into `SceneTreeDock`.\r\n\r\nReference to duplication code in `SceneTreeDock`: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/825ef2387f87de1c350696886e6c50b039204cef/editor/docks/scene_tree_dock.cpp#L879","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3239443829/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3239454643","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110112#issuecomment-3239454643","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110112","id":3239454643,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BFiez","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-08-30T18:49:27Z","updated_at":"2025-08-30T18:57:42Z","body":"I think your flipping of the undo/redo mechanism to focus on duplication instead of transform will solve that problem though. You would be letting the `SceneTreeDock` do all the work for undo/redo (which is just duplication). Undo/Redo for duplication stores a reference of the node including its transform, meaning that the transform of the node is \"saved\" regardless of when the undo/redo happened, it will still be correct. They shouldn't go back to the transform of the node(s) they were duplicated from because that information is actually NOT stored anywhere, which is the reverse of what one might expect.\r\n\r\nDuplicate (ref created) and added to Undo/Redo -> Transform (ref updated), skip creating undo/redo action for transform -> Undo (ref'ed node removed) -> Redo (ref'ed node restored with its correct transform i.e  wherever it was last located). ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3239454643/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3241670838","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110112#issuecomment-3241670838","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110112","id":3241670838,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BN_i2","user":{"login":"winston-yallow","id":44872771,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODcyNzcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44872771?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow","html_url":"https://github.com/winston-yallow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-01T09:49:48Z","updated_at":"2025-09-01T09:50:47Z","body":"I am not sure if I understand what you mean completely. Do you suggest to create the undo/redo already when the transform is started? My issue is that I don't want to create two history actions for what feels like one action from the user, so the duplication must happen on transform start, while the history commit must happen on transform end (when the new transform is known). That way there is only a single history entry. Letting the scene tree dock handle the undo/redo would mean to either have the history entry at transform start when the nodes are duplicated, or changing the scene tree dock logic quite a bit to split duplication and undo/redo logic.\r\n\r\nIn any case I'll take another look and try to make the duplication logic in `SceneTreeDock` reusable in some way. I will convert this PR to a draft for now as I won't have time to work on this before the next weekend, plus this is unlikely to go into 4.5 so there is a lot of time to work on this anyway.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3241670838/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3244753265","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110112#issuecomment-3244753265","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110112","id":3244753265,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7BZwFx","user":{"login":"ryevdokimov","id":105675984,"node_id":"U_kgDOBkx80A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/105675984?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov","html_url":"https://github.com/ryevdokimov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ryevdokimov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-02T10:33:59Z","updated_at":"2025-09-02T10:33:59Z","body":"I took a look a little bit more, and yeah, I can see it getting tricky specifically with cancelling. The undo/redo itself works fine when using `SceneTreeDock`, but as you mentioned we don't want to add the duplication to the undo history when the shift + transform begins. \r\n\r\nI just wonder what would happen is this functionality was desired in 2D as well. It becomes a tradeoff between complexity in `SceneTreeDock` and duplication in a few classes. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3244753265/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3649863810","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110112#issuecomment-3649863810","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110112","id":3649863810,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7ZjICC","user":{"login":"alazifk","id":93336644,"node_id":"U_kgDOBZA0RA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/93336644?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/alazifk","html_url":"https://github.com/alazifk","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alazifk/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alazifk/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alazifk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alazifk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alazifk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alazifk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alazifk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alazifk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/alazifk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-13T22:18:31Z","updated_at":"2025-12-13T22:18:31Z","body":"I think `SPACE` might be a better choice of key if possible.\r\n1. `SHIFT` is used to toggle snapping (unless this is being changed). You might want to toggle snapping _and_ duplicate at the same time.\r\n2. This being a high frequency action, it might be ergonomically nicer to use a strong finger instead of the pinky.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3649863810/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3649994231","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110112#issuecomment-3649994231","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110112","id":3649994231,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Zjn33","user":{"login":"winston-yallow","id":44872771,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ0ODcyNzcx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/44872771?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow","html_url":"https://github.com/winston-yallow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/winston-yallow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-14T00:44:04Z","updated_at":"2025-12-14T00:51:01Z","body":"I would prefer to keep it as Shift:\r\n1. The default toggle for snapping is control in the default \"Godot\" navigation scheme, so it does not interfere by default. If you do use an alternate navigation scheme, then snapping is still possible: Copy is determined while initiating the transform, while snapping is determined while placing. So you can still copy an object by holding shift down while starting the drag. And you can still snap the object by holding shift down while moving the object around. These work independently.\r\n2. I personally find holding space down more annoying, but probably also because I am not used to it and don't have muscle memory for it. Shift on the other hand is more widely used as an action modifier in general but also specifically for copying (for example the Source 2 level editor Hammer uses Shift for copy too)\r\n3. The 2D viewport uses space for panning. If we want to implement this feature for 2D too then it would be nice to have a consistent modifier for this, which Shift can be.\r\n4. Implementing this for space is a bit more involved. It's not impossible, but using modifier keys is a lot nicer to work with compared to multi-key presses to keep the code clean and maintainable.\r\n\r\nOn another note, I think I'll have some time around the turn of the year. Hopefully I can finally improve the undo/redo system by making at least some code from the SceneTreeDock reusable (and rebase the PR in the process)","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3649994231/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":3,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4076089908","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110112#issuecomment-4076089908","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110112","id":4076089908,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7y9DI0","user":{"login":"Copperplate","id":16230743,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjMwNzQz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16230743?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate","html_url":"https://github.com/Copperplate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copperplate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T16:00:15Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T16:05:09Z","body":"Now this would definitely be an amazing feature to have! Glad to see there is work being done on this. **EDIT:** In 2D, holding Alt has no currently assigned effect, whereas Shift and Ctrl both activate snapping modes. Perhaps Alt could still be utilized?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4076089908/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4513283585","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/110112#issuecomment-4513283585","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110112","id":4513283585,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABDQM-AQ","user":{"login":"Marks20125","id":108996807,"node_id":"U_kgDOBn8oxw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/108996807?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marks20125","html_url":"https://github.com/Marks20125","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marks20125/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marks20125/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marks20125/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marks20125/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marks20125/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marks20125/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marks20125/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marks20125/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Marks20125/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-21T22:29:24Z","updated_at":"2026-05-21T22:29:24Z","body":"Just wanted to say coming from UE5 I really miss this feature, I'd love to see it implemented","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4513283585/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]